From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cq8725s-ayn-odin3: charge LED follows charging state

The three LED channels on the PM8550 LPG (reg 1-3, as in the stock
Android devicetree) had no DT node, so the charge LED never lit.
Declare them as one RGB multi-led with the power-supply
battery-charging-orange-full-green trigger: orange while charging,
green when full, with no userspace involved.

The trigger name follows the battery power supply, which 0503
(ROCKNIX battery-name) names "battery". Channel 4 stays the fan PWM
(pwm-fan's <&pm8550_pwm 3 ...> in the common dtsi).

Ported from armada-os/armada 7f36e760ce70 ("feat(kernel): drive the
Odin 3 charge LED from charging state", PR #764), where it is part of
their dts/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts.patch.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
@@ -394,3 +394,29 @@
 			"DMIC3", "MIC BIAS3",
 			"TX SWR_INPUT6", "DMIC3_OUTPUT";
 };
+
+&pm8550_pwm {
+	multi-led {
+		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_RGB>;
+		function = LED_FUNCTION_CHARGING;
+		linux,default-trigger = "battery-charging-orange-full-green";
+
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <0>;
+
+		led@1 {
+			reg = <1>;
+			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_RED>;
+		};
+
+		led@2 {
+			reg = <2>;
+			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_GREEN>;
+		};
+
+		led@3 {
+			reg = <3>;
+			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_BLUE>;
+		};
+	};
+};
